To retrieve the interfaces for a GraphQL endpoint, you can use the introspection query. Introspection is a feature in GraphQL that allows you to query the schema of the GraphQL API and retrieve information about the available types, fields, and interfaces.

Here's an example of how you can retrieve the interfaces using the introspection query:

```graphql
query {
  __schema {
    types {
      name
      kind
      interfaces {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This query will return an object with the following structure:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "__schema": {
      "types": [
        {
          "name": "Query",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "MyInterface",
          "kind": "INTERFACE",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "MyObjectType",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": [
            {
              "name": "MyInterface"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "String",
          "kind": "SCALAR",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__Schema",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__Type",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__TypeKind",
          "kind": "ENUM",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__Field",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__InputValue",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__EnumValue",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__Directive",
          "kind": "OBJECT",
          "interfaces": []
        },
        {
          "name": "__DirectiveLocation",
          "kind": "ENUM",
          "interfaces": []
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

In this example, the `"MyInterface"` type is defined as an interface, and the `"MyObjectType"` type implements this interface.

You can use this information to understand the structure of the GraphQL schema and the available types, fields, and interfaces that you can query against.

